hipml 0.1.0

usage: hipml <command>

commands:
  probe     show the HIP device and how this binary was built
  kernels   list the kernel manifest
  vram      hipMemGetInfo now; --need BYTES also reports whether a cache fits
  parity    run every parity case (reference vs device); optional name filter
            --deep adds the 100K-context cases (slow host reference)
  bench     time each kernel launch and report effective bandwidth
  gguf      list the tensors in a GGUF file; `gguf <file> read <tensor>`
  decode-bench  stream every Q4_K/Q6_K/Q8_0 tensor through GEMV once
  generate  --gguf PATH --text "prompt" --tokens 20   greedy decode
            --device uses the chunked prefill graph (--chunk N, default 2048);
            --chunk 0 keeps the token loop; --compare-cpu compares the
            production chunk path (or --chunk 0) with the CPU oracle;
            --topk K prints the top-K log-probs at every sampled position
  load      load every tensor into VRAM and verify residency
  logits    run lm_head on a 5120-value f32 vector file
  prefill-bench  tiled prefill GEMM, Qwen3.8, M=512/2048
  prefill-model prefill the whole model cold, then warm from a KV prefix
  cache-bench cold / warm-exact / warm-shared TTFT on SSM+KV snapshots
  cache-gate  undersized-cap admission: refuse, miss, ids stay exact
  ssm       gated-delta-net parity (small + real layer) and layer timing
  attn-parity --gguf PATH   GPU full-attention block vs CPU reference
  attn-bench  --gguf PATH   per-layer time at depths 0/8192/100000
  gpu-bench --gguf PATH [--prefill N] [--depth D --kv q8]
  oracle-gate --gguf PATH --ids-file F --steps N  CPU oracle vs the
            production chunked path, step by step (exit 1 on a real split)
  splitk-gate --gguf PATH [--chunk 2048 --tails 40]  split-K ffn
            scratch vs HIPML_SPLITK=0 at every chunk tail
  gpu-profile --gguf PATH  launch cost, host round-trips, graph token
  bench-kv  quantized-KV decode attention: depth x q8/q4 x 1 head / 16 layers
            --depths 1024,8192,32768,100000 --reps 3
  rows-check --gguf PATH [--slots N --prefix P --tail T --decode D]
            multi-row tail prefill vs the single-sequence path
  serve     HTTP server: continuous batching, MTP, prefix cache

build with `--features hip` on a machine with the ROCm/HIP runtime.
